clueweb09-en0009-01-36176.0 Lipomas [livestrong.com] Lance Armstrong Foundation | Latest News: Groups posting issue fixed Register | Sign In [LIVESTRONG.COM - Health, Fitness & Lifestyle] [livestrong.com] LIVESTRONG The Daily Plate Members Home Get Healthy Fitness Diet & Nutrition Balance Appearance Lance Groups Forums The Daily Plate Dares Diseases and Conditions Treatments Drugs Symptoms Vitamins & Supplements Poisons Tests Mental Health Tools Home Get Healthy Diseases Diseases Articles 5 Things You Need to Know About Lipomas Overview Articles Videos 5 Things You Need to Know About Lipomas [Share] text size: | Post a comment | Print | [Add to my favorites] This Article has been added to your favorites. View your profile Featured Videos [video] Liver Disease Health Video [video] STD Health Video [video] Autoimmune Disorders Health Video 1. All Bumps are not Cancer Lipomas are fatty tumors. They are collections of fat set off from the tissue around them by a small membrane. They can be large or small and can occur anywhere there is subcutaneous fat. And they can scare the pants off someone when first discovered because they stick up like something that just HAS to be bad. They aren't. Unless their position or size causes pain, ignore them. A lipoma is
clueweb09-en0010-17-01556.0 Lipoma [Home] [Products] [Services] [Classes] [Information] [Search] [Shop Online] [Contact Us] [Lipoma] Lipoma (fatty tumor) Case Study Click button below to download PDF version of this web page, complete with hyperlinked references. [Lipoma PDF] Customer Service What is LIVE HolistiChat? [bullet] Statistics show that the life span of America's companion animals is now half what it was in the 1950's and 1960's. [bullet] Nearly 50 percent of natural deaths in older cats and dogs are attributed to cancer. To help prevent your pet from becoming a statistic, click on the happy dog below. Give your pet the fountain of youth and holistically help prevent cancer! For a FREE report on What Pet Food Companies Don't Want you to Know, sign up for our monthly e-newsletter. [] [Get Our Newletter] [] [] [] Tumors are unwanted whether benign (fatty tumors) or malignant (mast cell tumors). When fatty tumors appear, it is a sign the body is trying to get rid of unwanted material but because it is out of balance it can process this unwanted material through normal channels (kidneys, liver, intestines, etc.). Since the endocrine (glandular) and immune systems are usually not functioning at 100%, the body does the next best
